    "sectionTitle": {
      "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
      "description": "EP cables are an extension cord connecting EP catheters to the mapping or recording system. They are a set of insulated wires, wrapped in a protective coating, with unique connectors on each end. EP cables transmit the electrical signals sensed by the electrodes on a catheter to the EP recording and/or mapping system. Most are intended for sterile use in an electrophysiology lab. EP cables can be found in all EP labs, as well as some Cath labs, and are essential for every EP procedure performed. ",
      "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "user-73104d59b2@example.invalid",
